    "body": "Problem: The SQL LLM occasionally returns empty or incomplete SQL which causes downstream errors and makes evidence incomplete.\n\nSolution: Harden the SQL generation pipeline:\n- Prompt: canonical-only snake_case schema, symmetric LOWER rule, single micro-example, strict JSON-mode guidance.\n- Deterministic LLM call settings: low temperature, higher max_tokens, JSON-mode; provider errors return structured PROVIDER_ERROR.\n- Deterministic specialist bypass: for sales_performance and yoy_performance compose SQL without calling the SQL LLM; still emit sql_llm_prompt/sql_llm_output_raw placeholders and rails_status.specialist_bypass=true.\n- Metrics default: sales_performance defaults to ['dollar_sales','unit_sales','volume_sales'] when metrics tool returns empty.\n\nEvidence: The changes ensure top-level intermediates include plan, rails_status, sql, query_exec, sql_llm_prompt, sql_llm_output_raw, insights_llm_prompt, insights_llm_output.\n\nTests: Added focused tests for:\n- Specialist bypass \u2014 sales_performance (no SQL LLM call; specialist_bypass=true; fallback_used=false; final SQL includes filters + LIMIT 1000)\n- Specialist bypass \u2014 yoy_performance (emits base, _ya, delta, pct_delta; specialist_bypass=true)\n- Generalist success (SQL LLM returns valid JSON; evidence keys present)\n- Generalist incomplete (INCOMPLETE_SQL -> friendly error; preflight_complete=false)\n\nRisk: minimal. Specialist paths are deterministic; generalist path uses stricter prompt and JSON mode but behaviour is otherwise unchanged.\n\nDo not merge.  \n",
